---
import Base from "../../../../layouts/Base.astro";
import LegalDraft from "../../../../components/LegalDraft.astro";
---
<Base title="Privacy policy | doorbell.life" description="doorbell.life sets no cookies, writes nothing to browser storage and keeps no visitor IP addresses. Here is what we do process." noindex>
  <main>
    <h1>Does doorbell.life collect my data?</h1>
    <LegalDraft en />
    <p class="lead">Almost none. doorbell.life sets no cookies, writes nothing to browser storage, keeps no visitor IP addresses and never uses your IP address to guess where you are. The exceptions and details are below.</p>

    <h2>When you see a doorbell.life card on another site's error page</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your browser downloads the widget, its stylesheet and the day's data from cdn.doorbell.life. As with any web request, the connection reveals your IP address and browser type to the server. We do not keep them.</li>
      <li>Your region is worked out from your browser's time zone, inside your browser.</li>
      <li>Impression counts: one in ten displays sends two things, the site's domain and the topic shown, so we can count impressions per site and topic. Nothing about you is sent.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>When you browse doorbell.life</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The site currently has no analytics, no ads and sets no cookies.</li>
      <li>If we later place Google AdSense on article pages (ads may use cookies), we will update this policy before that starts. The widget, error-page templates and all missing-person pages will never carry ads.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Two exceptions that stay on your device</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>"Sort by my location" in the Taiwan vet directory</strong>: your browser asks for your location only after you press the button. Distances are calculated on your device; your location is not sent to us and not stored.</li>
      <li><strong>The pet-care practice game</strong>: your game progress is stored in your own browser. It contains only game progress, nothing that identifies you, and is never sent to us. Clearing your browser data deletes it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Missing-person and animal data</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Cards show data from government open data and from the agencies that publish it. We show only fields the source makes public and add nothing.</li>
      <li>Missing-person cases never get static pages and are never cached for offline pages; those pages are marked noindex and noarchive. When the source removes a case, it disappears from every error page.</li>
      <li>If you are the person in a case, or family, and want it removed, email contact@doorbell.life.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Information you choose to give us</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Email to contact@doorbell.life is used only to reply to you.</li>
      <li>GitHub issues and contributions are public. Please don't include personal information.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Service providers</h2>
    <p>The site and CDN are delivered by Cloudflare and the source code is hosted on GitHub. They process connection data under their own privacy policies.</p>

    <h2>Who runs this</h2>
    <p>doorbell.life is currently run by its maintainer as an individual. Questions: contact@doorbell.life. Updates to this policy will be dated on this page.</p>
  </main>
</Base>
